gpt.md:21:[COPIED-AUTHORITY] The calculator selects targets with \(|\bar y|\ge0.02\), compares prediction and target signs, pools held-out rows once per seed, and averages three seed metrics. It requires Spearman ≥0.20, raw accuracy ≥0.60, and raw advantage ≥0.05, alongside world-stability requirements (`fast-screen/compute_fit_screen.py`, lines 49–53, 95–164).
gpt.md:53:[INFERENCE] “Observable” requires leakage-free held-out information beyond matched placebo; “learnable” requires the fixed student to meet cross-world predicates; “composable” requires successful literal full-roster selection and service guards. “Efficacious” requires separately admitted physical policy comparisons with genuine retrained source ablations. Oracle signs, checksums, and fit associations establish none of that final efficacy claim (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§7–14).
gpt.md:98:[PROPOSAL] **Population and pairing.** Reserve ordered TRAIN worlds `2026121731`–`2026121738`, conditional on an authenticated ledger proving them unopened. These are proposed identifiers, not verified-unused assets; absent proof blocks admission, without automatic substitution. Exclude previous R6/V0.22 and reserved contingency worlds. Preserve lineage `2026092101`, rung `003000`, the exact checkpoint digest in gate §2.1, and seeds `2026135101`–`2026135103`. Pair arms within world/fold/seed. Retain anchors 1–9, outcome-blind pair enumeration, eight leave-one-world-out folds, and 32 common-field draws. Field keys exclude arm, pair, and profile.
gpt.md:100:[PROPOSAL] **Method and comparators.** Preserve LC-SRS, \(\lambda=118424222.8550065\) bit/J, \(\kappa=10097071012.757404\) bits, their frozen hexadecimal representations, C3View, 67–64–64–1 scorer, optimizer, S/R/C loss, and 2,000 updates. Fit INFORMED and MATCHED-PLACEBO only: 48 models. Retain ZERO-SURFACE \(B=Q1+Q2\) and TEACHER-ORACLE diagnostics. Preserve gate §7’s training-world strata, cyclic permutations, unchanged held-out labels, and ≥80% placebo eligibility per fold. No sign-reweighted training or candidate variants.
gpt.md:114:[PROPOSAL] **One acceptance rule.** Require informed Spearman ≥0.20, original raw accuracy ≥0.60, original raw advantage ≥0.05, **and** \(BA_I\ge0.60\), \(BA_I-BA_P\ge0.05\). Preserve informed mean-seed Spearman superiority in ≥6/8 worlds and each informed seed’s nonnegative Spearman in ≥5/8 worlds. These are operational thresholds, not significance levels. Report original row-pooled/seed-averaged raw metrics, equal-world balanced metrics, confusion counts, exclusions, and paired world/seed results. Worlds—not rows, draws, or initialization seeds—are physical clusters. No post-outcome metric or aggregation choice.
gpt.md:116:[PROPOSAL] **Physical/composition/service conjunction.** Retain gate §§10–12: ≥24 pairs and ≥1/world; ≥90% passing complete per-draw mechanics, with no unresolved formula, common-field, mask, or mutation errors; positive pooled 11-versus-00 EE and ≥4/8 positive worlds. Require action change ≥10%, literal 11 ≥25% and present in ≥4/8 worlds, harmful partials ≤5%, and topology consistency ≥80% among selected-11 pairs; zero selected-11 denominator fails. Oracle and informed full-roster EE must each exceed B pooled and in ≥4/8 worlds. Every world must satisfy \(S_I\ge S_B-0.01\). Preserve nonmember destination persistence, source-closure/no-new-destination checks, negative controls, identity tolerance, and bits/energy/lower-tail-service receipts. Pool physical totals separately per seed before averaging seed-level ratios; retain the frozen direction tolerances.
gpt.md:118:[PROPOSAL] **Preregistration and provenance.** Obtain timestamped controller acceptance before any fresh outcome. Bind contract, access ledger, physical source/runtime/TLE closure, Q12 observation-event ancestry, full anchor-record and surface digest domains, targets/profiles, field keys, masks, permutations, folds, initialization/configuration, and verifier. Authenticate production-path correction and composition-replay regressions first. Retain independent C1/C2 context predicates from gate §9: missing authentication is invalidity; a valid weak diagnostic is HOLD, not C3 rescue.
gpt.md:126:[PROPOSAL] Distinguish failed physics as a mechanism falsifier, failed held-out discrimination as an observability/learner falsifier, and successful discrimination with failed adoption/service as an interface-composition falsifier. None automatically means “C3 is impossible.”
